  "review": [
    "Both complete source figures and five prototype views directly inspected.",
    "Joint arrangement agrees qualitatively: screw on upper ear, lever on lower ear, swivel and nut below spring, rod eye at lever foot.",
    "The 24 mm radial stand-off prototype failed 64 local material pairs. Increasing the estimated stand-off to 38 mm passes 996 pairs while leaving all inherited occurrence frames unchanged.",
    "The wider stand-off moves the front pivots forward of the drawn centers; track linkage remains visibly low under the retained frame registration. These residuals are not scan-error proof and are not hidden by overlay realignment.",
    "Paired lug and eye widths, spring section/turns, swivel retention, threads and cast/forged transitions remain estimates. No stress, adjustment range or removal sequence has been qualified.",
    "M343/MX88 stop hardware and support bars, control rods and high-speed brakes remain absent."
  ],
